Subject: [gentoo-alpha] The end of compaq java. Current Gentoo/Alpha java situation.
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=flowed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-Archives-Salt: b99e84e9-5b96-446a-b952-938add101aae
X-Archives-Hash: 23943fd56324dec35a75f125a05fc938

Dear alpha crew:

After the last modification to our Gentoo/Java virtual system (bug
#138747) , the completely disappeared upstream support (from years ago),
the  problems and bugs related to compaq jdk/jre ebuilds (see bugs:
#84306, #110611, etc) and the fact of a 1.3 vm is quite obsolete
nowadays, the Gentoo/Alpha port have decided to drop the support (hard 
masking ATM) for compaq-jre,compaq-jdk.

This means we currently haven't got a full working java (==
virtual/{jre,jdk} provider) for the alpha arch.

Not all is lost, since other ways are open to get a valid and working
java environment for alpha. Kaffe and Sablevm seem to be the best
choices now:

  - Kaffe: testing tinderbox [1] is running (thanks to tcort).
  - SableVm: tcort and myself were testing it some time ago and last
results seems to be pretty good. Ebuilds are in the tree (just the
virtual machine) and in gentooexperimental[2].

If someone wants to hack a bit on this issue, setting up an overlay and
start working on it could be the best way and we'll be pleased to know
the results.

Wkr,

--
Jose Luis Rivero [yoswink@gentoo.org]
Gentoo/Doc Gentoo/Alpha


[1] Tinderbox
  - http://cs.ubishops.ca/~tcort/builder/

[2] SableVM-sdk
http://gentooexperimental.org/svn/java/gentoo-java-experimental/dev-java/sablevm-sdk/
-- 
gentoo-alpha@gentoo.org mailing list


